From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mario Limonciello <mario.limonciello@amd.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 13:51:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] xf86drmMode: validate event length in drmHandleEvent

drmHandleEvent walks the buffer returned by read() by advancing the
offset with i += e->length, where e->length is taken directly from the
buffer contents. Nothing validated this length, allowing a malformed or
untrusted event stream to misbehave:

  - e->length == 0 causes the offset to never advance, producing an
    infinite loop.
  - e->length < sizeof(struct drm_event) leaves fewer bytes than the
    header, so the next iteration casts a struct drm_event that straddles
    the end of the buffer.
  - e->length larger than the bytes remaining makes the handlers and the
    next cast read past the end of the buffer.

Validate that a full struct drm_event fits in the remaining bytes, and
that the event length is at least sizeof(struct drm_event) and does not
exceed the bytes remaining. When validation fails, log the specific error
via drmMsg() and return -1 to signal the caller that event processing
failed. This helps diagnose kernel bugs or corrupted event streams rather
than silently skipping or causing undefined behavior.

Signed-off-by: Mario Limonciello <mario.limonciello@amd.com>
---
 xf86drmMode.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xf86drmMode.c b/xf86drmMode.c
index d449343..5b5d705 100644
--- a/xf86drmMode.c
+++ b/xf86drmMode.c
@@ -1033,6 +1033,23 @@ drm_public int drmHandleEvent(int fd, drmEventContextPtr evctx)
 	i = 0;
 	while (i < len) {
 		e = (struct drm_event *)(buffer + i);
+		if (len - i < (int)sizeof(*e)) {
+			fprintf(stderr, "drmHandleEvent: incomplete event header at offset %d, len %d, sizeof(*e) %zu\n", i, len, sizeof(*e));
+			errno = EINVAL;
+			return -1;
+		}
+		if (e->length < sizeof(*e)) {
+			fprintf(stderr, "drmHandleEvent: event length %u smaller than header size %zu\n",
+			       e->length, sizeof(*e));
+			errno = EINVAL;
+			return -1;
+		}
+		if (e->length > (uint32_t)(len - i)) {
+			fprintf(stderr, "drmHandleEvent: event length %u exceeds remaining buffer size %d\n",
+			       e->length, len - i);
+			errno = EINVAL;
+			return -1;
+		}
 		switch (e->type) {
 		case DRM_EVENT_VBLANK:
 			if (evctx->version < 1 ||
